r_4_threat_and_current_target_hybrid = element "4-threat-and-current-target-hybrid" "SectionNote" {
    tags "SectionNote,Overview"
    properties {
        "id" "4-threat-and-current-target-hybrid"
        "kind" "SectionNote"
        "order" "63"
        "source.commit" "175e0c59b6a05ead62d29bd851085cd5a3818378"
        "source.status" "historical baseline coordinates"
        "source.file" "4_Relations.md"
        "source.start" "63"
        "source.end" "97"
        "title" "Threat and current target (hybrid)"
        "heading.level" "3"
        "heading.slug" "threat-and-current-target-hybrid"
        "section" "Overview"
        "note.001.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.001.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.001.text" "Owner-requested clarification (2026-09-18), documentation only. These relations describe the"
        "note.001.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.002.text" "approved mob/player scope. A **mob** is an individual non-player combat `entity`, not the shared"
        "note.001.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.003.text" "`creature` species definition; the player endpoint identifies an individual `player-character`."
        "note.001.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.004.text" "For threat/order retention, these are logical mob/player identities, not only currently spawned"
        "note.001.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.005.text" "nodes. Temporary absence and surviving-mob restart preserve the approved remaining state under"
        "note.001.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.006.text" "§3.2; `current-target` still requires a present, living player entity. Restart retention promises"
        "note.001.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.001.line.007.text" "no restored target node, chooses no storage strategy and adds no combat pairings."
        "note.001.source.file" "4_Relations.md"
        "note.001.source.start" "65"
        "note.001.source.end" "71"
        "note.002.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.002.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.001.text" "**Threat** is the directed mob → player relationship, not a separate global player stat."
        "note.002.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.002.text" "Its numeric property **`aggro-points`** measures the relationship's strength, in **aggro points**"
        "note.002.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.003.text" "(also called threat points). Each mob can track zero or more players and each player can have"
        "note.002.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.004.text" "incoming threat relations from zero or more mobs, independently. **`current-target`** identifies"
        "note.002.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.005.text" "at most one player that a mob is currently targeting; changing it does not erase other threat"
        "note.002.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.006.text" "relations. Ordinary selection uses that mob's own scores and the rules in §3.2 `ai-behavior`."
        "note.002.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.007.text" "Heroic Shout temporarily overrides `current-target`, not `threat`: it grants neither aggro"
        "note.002.line.008.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.008.text" "points nor engagement order, and taunt alone adds no neutral provocation or lasting eligibility."
        "note.002.line.009.state" "text"
        "note.002.line.009.text" "When it ends, ordinary targeting resumes unless protected return applies (§3.2)."
        "note.002.source.file" "4_Relations.md"
        "note.002.source.start" "73"
        "note.002.source.end" "81"
        "note.003.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.003.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.003.line.001.text" "Illustrative runtime facts, not static instance data or balance defaults:"
        "note.003.source.file" "4_Relations.md"
        "note.003.source.start" "83"
        "note.003.source.end" "83"
        "note.004.kind" "code"
        "note.004.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.001.text" "```text"
        "note.004.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.002.text" "mob-a --threat {aggro-points: 20}--> player-you"
        "note.004.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.003.text" "mob-a --threat {aggro-points: 30}--> player-teammate"
        "note.004.line.004.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.004.text" "mob-a --current-target-----------> player-teammate"
        "note.004.line.005.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.005.text" "mob-b --threat {aggro-points: 40}--> player-you"
        "note.004.line.006.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.006.text" "mob-b --current-target-----------> player-you"
        "note.004.line.007.state" "text"
        "note.004.line.007.text" "```"
        "note.004.source.file" "4_Relations.md"
        "note.004.source.start" "84"
        "note.004.source.end" "90"
        "note.005.kind" "paragraph"
        "note.005.line.001.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.001.text" "Pack membership is the generated grouping of mob individuals (§3.2), not `member-of-family`"
        "note.005.line.002.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.002.text" "or `belongs-to-faction`. Shared current sightings do not copy `threat`, engagement order or"
        "note.005.line.003.state" "text"
        "note.005.line.003.text" "`current-target`; each mob selects independently under §3.2. Open questions are in §7."
        "note.005.source.file" "4_Relations.md"
        "note.005.source.start" "92"
        "note.005.source.end" "94"
    }
}
